at the Quran uses وَمَآ أَدْرَاكَ مَا is used in the Quran 13 times Each of those times, the Quran refers to something unique So for instance, like ٱلْقَارِعَةُ (The Striking Hour) as you showed, which is one of the names of the Day of Judgment So it refers to a unique concept, that concept is the Day of Judgment", "We don't know how the Day of Judgment is going to be, We don't understand, we don't understand its significance, it's majesty, So the Quran brings your attention to that. So he talked, for example, about chapter:97 of the Quran or Surat alQadr You see in that chapter, it uses لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ (The Night of Decree). The word لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ it's used 3 times (alQadr97:1-3) The chapter, by the way, is 30 words, it's only 30 words! But it uses لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ three times in the chapter, which is already 6 words out of the 30 words And it maintains its eloquence and uniqueness.", "It uses it 3 times Now this word لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ or ٱلْقَدْر it's not used anywhere else in the Quran So I was talking to you about the uniqueness of the words used So each chapter of the Quran has a unique word that is only used once in that chapter, and not used anywhere else in the Quran, each chapter of the Quran has that So this chapter; chapter:97, has the word ٱلْقَدْر, it's not used anywhere Like I said, it's used 3 times in this chapter, it's not used anywhere else in the Quran So it's not used multiple times because you don't have other words to use, because it doesn't exist anywhere else in the Quran in 6,000 verses But the Quran highlights that it can use the same term multiple times and maintain the highest level of eloquence You look, for example, chapter:114 of the Quran (anNas).", "It uses the word ٱلْخَنَّاسِ (the retreating whisperer i.e. Satan) It's only used in that chapter, it's not used anywhere else in the Quran Chapter:113, ٱلْفَلَق (The Daybreak) (alFalaq113:1) Chapter:112, ٱلصَّمَد (The Eternal Refuge) (alikhlas112:2) Chapter:111, أَبِى لَهَبٍۢ (the name \"Abi Lahab\") (alMasad111:1) And I can go on and on. I go with every chapter of the Quran, and here are one word or more! because it doesn't have to even be one, that is only unique to that chapter in the Quran So you mentioned that chapter, لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ Then the Quran uses that expression, which you said, وَمَآ أَدْرَاكَ مَا How would you know what لَيْلَةِ ٱلْقَدْرِ is?", "So no one knew what لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ was. It's a complete new concept the Quran introduces, Which is this magnificent Night in the month of Ramadan, Which as the Quran describes it in the same chapter (alQadr97:3) خَيْرٌۭ مِّنْ أَلْفِ شَهْرٍۢ So (it is better than 1,000 months) Meaning the deed that you will do.. It's like you did that one deed for 1,000 months So you will do one action, one deed in that Night, you will times it x 1,000 months That's how magnificent that Night is! So Muslims usually, typically in Ramadan, try to do their best in this Night, so they can account, or get the most amount of blessings and rewards as much as they can within that Night, Because it's a magnificent Night Then the Quran highlights how magnificent it is by the angels descending in that Night Another example, this word ٱلْقَدْر The Arabs always use this word ٱلْقَدْرِ to mean the مكانة of someone", "– the stature of someone But how the Quran introduces a complete new meaning now to this word ٱلْقَدْرِ to mean judgment, The Night of Decree or Night of Judgment So it adds a complete new meaning to the wordٱلْقَدْرِ and it links it to قَدَر and مقادير and \"writing the actions of the people\" So it links it to Judgment and Accountability and the Decree of the actions of people Because in that Night, the actions of the people of the entire year -the decree- is determined. That's why it's the Night of Decree So it became الحُكم there.", "So it became a Decree, instead of it was the stature of an individual And it's clearly understood by the Arabs So the Quran introduced a previous word; ٱلْقَدْر which means مكانة (makana: status) That the Arabs knew to mean that And the Quran introduces a complete new meaning, And then it links it to this new Night that you've never known or heard about And then it introduces a new structure and linguistic expression وَمَآ أَدْرَاكَ مَا to signify its importance. And all of that is in one verse And then you get someone like this, who doesn't understand anything, like I said, about the Arabic language, then comes and criticises the concept \"And how would you know what that concept is in the future?\"", "You don't even understand! If you don't understand Arabic, you don't understand linguistic structures, then why are you talking -with all due respect-? Like you shouldn't be talking about any of these things You're not educated enough, you don't understand",))
