an down and he told him where to place these specific verses through the Revelation There was multitude of different people who are called -specifically- كتبة الوحي (Writers of Revelation) These people were people the Prophetﷺ selected, and whenever the Quran came down, he called one of them to come and write the Quran One of them is for example: Zayd ibn Thabit, Uthmanؓ -we mentioned-, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, Ubay ibn Ka'bؓ Multiple different Companions of the Prophetﷺ.", "There were many many companions and their job was to write down the Quran They were writing the Quran on any parchment: leather, rocks, wood, whatever was available at that time Because at that time papers were not available in the Deserts of Arabia, so they were writing down on parchments Wherever they could find, any part.. Whenever the Quran is revealed they bring a piece of leather, piece of wood, whatever it is Then they write the Quran down on that piece. And some of the Companions of the Prophetﷺ also had their own personal books Where they were writing some of the Quran and they were writing also their interpretations, their understanding It was a mixture between the revelation of the Quran as well as their understanding etc.", "And we'll come to that point later on, so keep it in mind that some of the Companions had their own personal Books and مصاحف (Masahif: copies of the Quran) where they had the Quran as well as explanation/understanding. For example, 'Aishaؓ she had the Quran and one of the verses of the Quran she was saying حَـٰفِظُوا۟ عَلَى ٱلصَّلَوَٰتِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱلْوُسْطَىٰ ((صلاة العصر)) (Observe the prayers; especially the middle prayer) ((Asr Prayer)) So there was an extra part there that she was adding as an interpretation in her own personal مُصْحَف (Mushaf: copy of Quran) as well as Ubay ibn Ka'b and many of the other companions, they also had their own personal Masahif that they used to write interpretation as well as the Quran also in these Masahif",))
