am spread very fast. I'm not sure if you know or not. Islam spread very very very fast. And then more and more more people came into Islam and then the number of of memorizers only increases. So, now we go from thousands to tens of thousands to hundreds of thousands to millions. Today we have millions of memorizers of the Quran. We have something a certificate which we call it is ijazah.", "The certificate has If I memorize the Quran, I have a certificate to have an ijazah. It has my name, then my teacher's name, then his teacher's name, all the way back to Prophet Muhammad. So the people who memorize the Quran, there's many people who memorize the Quran who don't have an ijazah, who don't even have the certificate. They still memorize it. But we have millions of people with certificates as well, with the names tracing back all the way to Prophet Muhammad. And this tradition we keep How do we keep this tradition alive? Every year, you know, in Ramadan, the month where we fast, in every mosque, if you go to majority of the mosques, we recite the entire Quran.", "The 30 parts of the Quran from beginning to end, we recite one part a day in the month, the 30 parts. Some mosques even recite two parts, and they finish it twice in the month. You go and you can listen to the entire Quran. Someone from memory, he's reciting it. And then if he makes any mistake, people behind him memorizing they correct him. Instantly. So this tradition of memorizing the Quran makes it impossible for anyone to change it. I'll give you a basic example. Now, the alphabet. You memorize the alphabet, I memorize the alphabet. Can anyone change the alphabet?", "No. Cuz there's millions of people who memorize the alphabet. People recite it in schools. It's way less than the Quran. The Quran is a lot more recited every day by Muslims. But I'm saying even the alphabet is a is a easy example. If I say e d c b, someone is going to say it's a b c d. Even the in the order of saying it, they will correct me. Cuz there's an order that is being taught that people learn that, and people memorize that. Now, imagine the Quran. Every Muslim recites the Quran in the prayer.", "And the Quran is being recited every year, like I said, in Ramadan, the whole of it. Parts are always being recited all over the world in every prayer. But, the whole thing is also being recited off by heart in Ramadan. So, we have this main method of preservation, which is why we know even if you take every book and throw it in the sea. Now, imagine right now we just do this experiment and we'll throw every religious literature in the sea. The only religious literature that is going to come back is the Quran. Cuz it's the only religious literature that you can reproduce from memory.", "Nobody memorizes the entire Bible. No, we I haven't even met a single person that memorizes an entire gospel, one gospel. Let alone the New Testament or the Old Testament or the entire Bible. So, it's the only religion that has this tradition as Muslims, okay? So, that's more than enough to show that the Quran is being preserved.",))
