#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("When these companions travelled, and people learned from them at the time of the Caliph of Islam Uthmanؓ there were certain wars taking place, so armies were coming from different lands Now, when these armies came from different lands there was a problem happening here Because, as we said, these companions had their own Qiraa and in these lands people were learning from the companions So, if Abdullah ibn 'Abbas was in one land and Umar ibn al-Khattab was in a different land the people in this land learned from Abdullah ibn 'Abbas his Qiraa, and the people here learned from Umar ibn al-Khattab When the time of war came, and the people came from this land the people came from this land Now they have two different Qiraat, now they have two different recitations, because they took from two different companions even though it's all Quran, but the choices that these companions made from the 7 Ahruf is different", "They will end up reciting the Quran slightly differently from the other companion that is coming from the other land When these armies met people started disagreeing with each other They're saying to each other: \"What is this? This is not the Quran that I was listening to!\" and this happens even today, if some Muslims -today- go, for example, to certain parts of the world, to Morocco and they are reciting the recitation of Hafs, and they start listening to Warsh then they don't recognize many of the words are being said, so they think something is wrong here if you're not aware..", "And these were new Muslims bear in mind, because Islam spread far and wide, so a lot of them were new Muslims They were not aware of the 7 Ahruf and they were not aware of the concept of Qiraat Then there were disagreements happening between the people Hudhayfa ibn alYaman came to Uthmanؓ and he said that the people are disagreeing about the Qiraat There's a problem happening here, people are disagreeing with each other because they learned from different companions their Qiraa Now they're not understanding why someone else is reciting a different way Even though all of these ways of recitation are in the end revelation coming from Allahﷻ So, what Uthmanؓ did is he consulted the Companions and then he made a committee, and he made a standardised text of the Quran Why did he make a standardised text of the Quran?", "So he can send them to these lands and then say to the people that \"Look..\" \"Whatever you're reciting has to be restricted to the standardised version of the Quran\" What this standardised version of the Quran does is two things First, it restricts the recitations of the people, the choices that they can make to that standardised version of the Quran and then if there is any disagreement they can always come back to that specific standardised version of the Quran Where did this standardised version come from? What Uthmanؓ did is he brought the same person, Zayd ibn Thabit Who Abu Bakr made compile the Quran in the stage that we spoke about before he brought the same person Zayd ibn Thabit, and he brought that compiled Quran that was written at the time of the Prophetﷺ, his life and he used it to make that standardised text, the standardised version of the Quran", "Then he did not put any diacritical marks so people can recite multitude of different recitations of the Quran using that same text It's one text but you can recite in different modes, different Qiraat. You can use different Qiraat to recite the same text That standardised text that was based on the same Quran that was written down at the time of the Prophetﷺ in accordance with the final revelation that was revealed, then what Uthman did is he sent it to the different lands, he sent the standardised text to different lands and then told the people that if they want to recite the Quran they have to stick to that specific text It does not have diacritical marks, so it can include multitude of different recitations, but you are still restricted to whatever is in the text You cannot go anywhere else, you're restricted to that specific text", "so, it kind of restricted the full 7 Ahruf, so it's not all of them right now, there is a restricted version of the 7 Ahruf Something that is very important to understand here is that any Harf is enough, as the Prophetﷺ said كلُّها شافٍ كافٍ (Each Harf of it is enough) if we just have one recitation or one Harf of the Quran, that is enough for people because all of it is Quran in the end, and all of it is the 114 different chapters but it's just different ways of reciting these 114 different chapters So, that skeletal text of Uthmanؓ that does not have diacritical marks you can have multitude of different Qiraat that you can use to read that specific text but as we said, something VERY important to understand.", "They never learned the Quran from the text which is why Uthmanؓ left it without diacritical marks, because you cannot just pick it up and start reading a specific recitation The learning was always oral, and the text was always secondary The purpose of the text is two things; to combine the people at one text, and if there is any disagreement they can come back to it that was the only reason Uthmanؓ made that standard text, and then what Uthmanؓ also did is he burnt any other copies Now, what copies did he burn? He burned these personal Masahif that we mentioned in the beginning We said in the beginning different companions had their own personal Masahif, and they had interpretation in there, etc.", "So, what Uthmanؓ did, he said: \"Bring any of these Masahif, personal Masahif of the people, we're going to remove them.\" We're just going to leave that standard text, so people can come back to it and do not go to multitude of different sources Only one source to come back to Now, a very important point to note here as well, is we mentioned the Quran or the parchments that were written at the time of the Prophetﷺ, his life These parchments were still preserved, even after Uthman made the standard text. These parchments were there, Uthmanؓ did not burn this original If you want to call it \"Original\".", "He did not burn these original parchments in fact He made the standardised version, he burned the personal Masahif, but he did not burn these parchments that were written at the time of the Prophetﷺ They remained until 50 to 60 A.H, which is like 20 or 30 years later after Uthmanؓ But he didn't burn at that time, they were still available. All he did is that he made a standard text with the agreement of all of the companions Like Aliؓ said: \"whatever Uthman did was under the supervision of all of us.\" So, it was not a personal decision that Uthmanؓ made Uthmanؓ and all of the 4 Caliphs the Prophetﷺ told us to follow their way and their tradition So, that standard text was then made, and then it solved this idea of disagreement of different people coming from different parts of the land disagreeing on different recitations that they took from the companions", "So now, the people are restricted to the text, but there are still many recitations that you can recite using that text because the text does not have diacritical marks. You can recite \"مَلِكِ\", you can recite \"مَـٰلِكِ\", you can recite \"تَبَيَّنُوا\", you can recite \"تَثَبَّتُوا\" and you can recite these different words using the same text, you can say \"وَٱلضُّحَىٰ\", you can say [وَٱلضُّحي] There were still tons of different Qiraat available, but people are still restricted to one skeletal text that they come back to When it comes to the recitations of the Quran. This was the third stage of the recitations of the Quran and the preservation of the text The final stage of the recitations of the Quran.",))
