#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Now, after we said there's a skeletal text, which is the text that Uthmanؓ standardised and he sent to different lands, and there's as we said tons of different Qiraat that people took from the companions and then from their students. The companions combined from the 7 Ahruf and then their students combined from different Companions Then the students of the students combined from different students and all of it is combining from Revelation Coming with different Qiraat, so there was a multitude of different Qiraat Later on in history, there was an individual called ibn Mujahid, and ibn Mujahid was a scholar in the Quran and recitations of the Quran What ibn Mujahid did, is he looked at where are the best recitations of the Quran There's a multitude of different recitations, so let me look at the best reciters, the people who are most eloquent in their recitation", "Most eloquent in their understanding of the of the Arabic language Have the best chains tracing back to the Prophetﷺ, the most authentic chains What he did is he took 7 of these recitations, and he wrote a book about these 7 different recitations He took 7 different recitations not the Ahruf, he said: \"The Ahruf are different\" a recitation is combining between different Ahruf or recitations of the companions He collected in that book 7 recitations. Not 7 Ahruf, 7 recitations, and that book of the 7 recitations He collected the most eloquent and the best recitations that he found at the time People did not have to follow that book, did not have to take information from that book That was just a personal decision that he made, ibn Mujahid.", "This was not like \"Muslims have to follow this!\" or something There were still many other different recitations that people were reciting and taking, but what happened later on is that book became so popular and then the people started restricting themselves to these 7 different recitations and a lot of people had a misconception, they thought that the 7 recitations of ibn Mujahid are the same as the 7 Ahruf which we've already highlighted they're completely two different things. And that's why many of the scholars blamed ibn Mujahid They said: \"He could have collected 8 recitations, or 6 recitations, or 20 recitations\" \"Why did he have to choose 7?\"", "Which confused many of the people thinking that these 7 recitations are the 7 Ahruf So, these 7 recitations became wildly popular among the people, among the population. People started reciting the 7 Ahruf of the Quran Some of the scholars also came later on and what they did.. To clear that misunderstanding as well They added 3 extra recitations from the eloquent reciters of the Quran, the people who have the best chains, etc. The most understanding of the Arabic language, and they added 3 extra recitations of the Quran Like Ibn al-Jazari in his book \"النشر في القراءات العشر\" Then we have 10 recitations, these 10 eloquent recitations Now as we said, these recitations are all what?", "They're combinations of the different Ahruf They're combinations of the revelation that came from the companions They're combinations from the oral text, and all of the oral text traces back to the Prophetﷺ with chains of narration The 10 recitations that we're reciting today, they were not the only recitations available, as we said There were tons of other recitations. The only reason that they are popular today is because they became popular later on People started adopting them because of their eloquence. People started following them and reciting them as well However, there were many many different recitations of the Quran and something interesting for people to understand is that even today if you become a scholar of Qiraat and highly eloquent in the Arabic language, etc.", "you can even have a new Qiraa, you can combine between these 10 different Qiraat So, even today you're not restricted to the 10 different Qiraat! Why? Because all of them are Quran, all of them are Revelation, all of them are coming from Allahﷻ All of them for us are considered Quran. These recitations of the Quran, the 10 different recitations of the Quran They are HIGHLY mass transmitted. We're talking about tens of thousands, hundreds of thousands of chains of narrations transmitting these 10 recitations of the Quran, tracing back to the Prophetﷺ and we have voluminous works that have the names and biographies of the people in the chain the people transmitting the information not the information itself, but just the people transmitting the information.", "Autobiographies of them, for example الضوء اللامع or الحلقات المضيئة or النشر في القراءات العشر or طبقات القراء All of these are books which contain the biographies of the narrators of the Quran and the chains themselves are available as well, you can see them in \"النشر في القراءات العشر\" and \"طبقات القراء\" Where you have a multitude.. We're talking about mass transmission Individuals in the chain reporting these 10 different eloquent Qiraat, tracing back to the Prophetﷺ Anyone today who recites any of the Qiraat has something which is called \"Ijaza\" I'm going to show an example of it on the screen.", "An Ijaza is.. You have a certificate, and this certificate has the names of your teachers of one of the 10 Qiraat that you recite, the names of your teachers going back all the way to the Prophetﷺ and today we have millions of these. Millions of memorisers of the Quran we have millions of certificates of Ijaza of people transmitting that same text Now it is very important to understand, that whichever Qiraa you recite the Quran with, it is considered Quran Because they are combinations from the 7 Ahruf which are all coming from Allahﷻ The purpose of them is to just make the Quran easy for people to memorise, easy for people to understand So today, we have this Mass transmission of hundreds of thousands..", "of millions of certificates of people transmitting these 10 different recitations of the Quran that we read So, there is not a shadow of a doubt when it comes to the oral preservation of the Quran is that these 10 recitations that we're reciting are Quran, and our combinations of the 7 Ahruf, is the Quran, the revelation that is coming from Allahﷻ So, when we say: \"The Quran is preserved letter for letter, word for word.\" Yes! it is preserved letter for letter, word for word because each of the recitations is Quran, and each letter and each vowel and each way to recite is Quran The Quran is preserved letter for letter, word for word, vowel for vowel and will always be preserved in that way Many people, they do not understand the concept of Ahruf and Qiraat, which causes confusion sometimes for people when they're perceiving the different recitations of the Quran.", "And now, when you understand the history behind it The history behind the development of the Qiraat, and that they are combinations of the Ahruf that were recited by the Prophetﷺ and were Revelation coming down directly from Allahﷻ and they were the same 114 Chapters with very slightly different dialects of recitation and differences that enrich and increase the meaning of the Quran",))
