is, even though he's denying He also knows that these signs are coming from the Creator. So that is enriching and increasing the meaning of the Quran Now, that's why you see Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who was actually one of the four people that the Prophetﷺ recommended that people take the Quran from, or take the recitations of the Quran from There's a Hadith of the Prophetﷺ he said: \"Take the Quran from 4 people..\"", "i.e. these four people are the best reciters So, one of them is Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Ubay ibn Ka'b, Muadh ibn Jabal, and Salim. These 4 people The Prophetﷺ said to take the Quran from them, they're the most eloquent in reciting Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said \"I've seen the reciters in the beginning..\" i.e., \"I've seen these different Ahruf, these different dialects of the Arab\" \"..these different Revelations that came from Allahﷻ, and they're very close! They're like هلُمَّ and أقْبِل\" Both of these two words mean the same thing They mean \"Come\" but it's just different ways to say the same thing and as we said different words that are also enriching the meaning like \"The King\" and \"The Owner\" This was essentially the 7 Ahruf, the 7 Ahruf were 7 dialects that also added more unique words that enrich the meaning of the Quran and unique ways of reciting certain words that add and increase the meaning of the Quran", "Now, the very important thing to understand here is that all of these different things are all considered Quran So, when we say \"there's only one Quran\" there's only one Quran! because that is the same text, but it is recited in different ways that is the same text, but these differences are all coming down from Allah so, Quran is the recitation of the text of the Revelation that comes from Allahﷻ, that's what the Quran is and all of these different Ahruf, all of these 7 Ahruf, all of these unique words like \"مَـٰلِكِ\" and \"مَلِكِ\", or \"عَلِمْتُ\" and \"عَلِمْتَ\", or \"تَبَيَّنُوا\" and \"تَثَبَّتُوا\" All of these are coming from 