nst this absurd theory is the orientalist claim held by the likes of Tisdall and Murad as well as contemporary Christian apologists that the prophet peace be upon him had access to the proto evangelium of James. Now if that's the case then the prophet peace be upon him surely would have noticed that both mediams have different fathers. In other words, the inclusion of Imran as the name of Miam's father was intentional. What I do find really funny though about this whole argument is that not only is the Quran mixing up mediams, but it is mixing up the mediums that cannot be confused.", "Mary was a very common name after all. In the New Testament, you have Mary the mother of Jesus, of course, Mary Magdalene, Mary of Bethany, Mary of Clus, Mary the mother of James and Joseph, and Mary the mother of John Mark. Now, the Quran doesn't confuse the mother of Jesus with any of the Marys found in first century Judea, but allegedly confuses her with a Mary from Egypt a thousand years earlier. So let's summarize all this quickly. One, the Quran refers to the father of Miam as Imran since his name was Imran and there is no evidence to contradict this.", "Two, the Quran refers to Miam as the sister of Harun not because she was the actual sister of Harun but because it was a common practice as per the hadith of the prophet peace be upon him. And three, there are several pieces of evidence that indicate that the Quran differentiated between both Miams. And there you have it, ladies and gents. And his challenge have been refuted. and a curt.",))
#source("Source: Farid Responds, \"[DEBUNKED] One Mistake Destroys Islam? - Challenge Accepted!\"")

