d, comes down with angels protecting it, and there is no way that any change could happen to it.", "It's impossible. Also, Allah told the Prophetﷺ, “When the revelation is told, do not hasten to recite it (TaHa20;114) First, internalise it. When you're done, Allah will preserve it in your heart, then recite it”. So it was not like these two verses came and the Prophetﷺ straight away said it because there is a way that Allah told the Prophetﷺ to accept and take the revelation. Now, on top of that as well, the place where you prostrate is actually in the end of the Surah, in the end of the chapter, it is not where the names of the idols are mentioned.", "So that is another reason that shows inconsistency to the story, right? So I can go on and on, just giving you pieces of evidence of why, from the Quran and from the Hadith and from the science of Hadith itself as well, looking at the narrations, this story is completely fabricated",))
